<task id="061" project="messaging-communication-app-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Package the polling timeline as a PCF (React 16/17 platform libs) + deploy to the OOB `sprk_communication`/thread form + UI tests</title>
    <phase>W6 — UI (polling timeline + PCF accessories)</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>8</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>060</dependencies>
    <blocks></blocks>
    <tags>pcf, deploy, e2e-test, dataverse</tags>
    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>Packages a shared-library component as a PCF (React 16/17 platform libraries per ADR-022) and DEPLOYS it to a live Dataverse form via solution ZIP import — an irreversible/host-affecting operation with prescriptive deploy steps; touches `.ts` PCF code + manifest + solution. ADR-022 (platform libs), ADR-006 (PCF for form binding), ADR-026 (Path-A exception) bind; UI tests gate the render. FULL required.</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W6</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>New PCF folder under `src/client/pcf/` + its own solution ZIP — disjoint from 062/063 file surfaces. Depends only on 060 (the component it wraps). Deploy targets a distinct control on the OOB form.</parallel-reason>
    <fr-refs>FR-10</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Package the `CommunicationTimeline` component (task 060) as a **PCF control** and deploy it to the OOB `sprk_communication` / communication-thread main form, so the polling timeline renders inside the model-driven app with no Code Page host.

    Requirements:
    - **PCF wrapper** in a NEW `src/client/pcf/CommunicationTimeline/` control. It is a virtual/React PCF that mounts `<CommunicationTimeline/>` from `@spaarke/ui-components`, wiring the PCF context to the component props: resolve `threadId` from the bound form record (the `sprk_thread` lookup / the thread record id), inject an `authenticatedFetch` built from the Spaarke PCF auth pattern (`@spaarke/auth` is consumed at the PCF boundary — NOT inside the shared component), and pass `bffBaseUrl` from an environment variable / control property.
    - **React 16/17 platform libraries** (ADR-022) — the PCF MUST use the platform-provided React (16/17), NOT bundle React 18. Confirm the control manifest declares platform libraries and the component tree is React-16/17-compatible (the timeline uses no React-18-only APIs that break under 16/17; if any slipped in via 060, coordinate a fix in the shared lib rather than forking).
    - **Solution packaging + deploy** — build production mode with `npm run build:prod` (NOT `npm run build` — AP-1), pack a solution ZIP, and import to the target environment via the `pcf-deploy` skill. Place the control on the OOB form.
    - **No client-side ACS SDK** — the packaged bundle MUST NOT contain any `@azure/communication-*` dependency (NFR-04); the timeline reads persisted records via the BFF only.
    - **UI tests** — verify the control renders on the form without console errors, is dark-mode correct, and reflects a new inbound message within one poll cycle.

    Do NOT build the send/respond accessory PCFs here (task 062) or the quoting action (task 063) — this task packages + deploys the timeline VIEWER only.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke PCF engineer fluent in the virtual/React PCF pattern, ADR-022 platform libraries (React 16/17), the `pcf-deploy` solution-ZIP workflow, and the PCF `@spaarke/auth` boundary idiom. Familiar with the email-r4 `CommunicationActions`/`CommunicationConnections` PCFs as the packaging + form-placement precedent.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A `CommunicationTimeline` PCF exists in `src/client/pcf/`, mounts the shared component, resolves `threadId`/`authenticatedFetch`/`bffBaseUrl` from PCF context, uses React 16/17 platform libraries (ADR-022), builds clean via `npm run build:prod`, packs a solution ZIP, and is deployed to the OOB `sprk_communication`/thread form via `pcf-deploy`. The bundle contains no ACS SDK. UI tests confirm it renders without console errors, is dark-mode correct, and reflects a new inbound message within one poll cycle.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      ADR-026 Path-A exception (spec §ADR Tensions): R1's message surface is the OOB main form + PCFs (mirroring email-r4's shipped W4 pivot) — NOT a Code Page. A form-bound PCF is within ADR-006 (PCF for form binding). This task realizes that surface for the timeline viewer; cite the Path-A exception in the deploy PR.

      §11 Component Justification: the PCF wrapper is justified because the shared `CommunicationTimeline` component cannot mount on an MDA form by itself — a PCF is the only host that binds it to a `sprk_communication`/thread record and supplies the PCF auth context. The concrete failure mode without it is that FR-10's "usable message experience inside the MDA" has no delivery vehicle. It does not overlap the accessory PCFs (062, which are send/respond actions) — this is the read/timeline surface. Reuse the email-r4 `CommunicationActions` PCF's `@spaarke/auth` boundary + manifest + solution structure rather than inventing a new packaging.

      ADR-022 boundary: the shared component (060) is authored React-18-friendly for the lib, but PCFs run on the platform React (16/17). The PCF wrapper must declare platform libraries and the mounted tree must be 16/17-safe. If a React-18-only API is present, fix it in the shared lib (coordinate with 060) — do NOT fork the component into the PCF.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/client/pcf/CommunicationTimeline/ (NEW — control folder: index.ts, ControlManifest.Input.xml, solution)</file>
      <file>src/client/pcf/CommunicationActions/ (READ — email-r4 PCF: @spaarke/auth boundary, manifest, solution ZIP structure to mirror)</file>
      <file>src/client/pcf/CommunicationConnections/ (READ — virtual PCF + view/solution packaging precedent)</file>
      <file>src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CommunicationTimeline/ (CONSUME — the component packaged here)</file>
      <file>src/client/pcf/CLAUDE.md (READ — PCF module rules)</file>
      <file>docs/guides/PCF-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md (READ — deploy workflow)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-10">The timeline is packaged as a PCF and deployed to the OOB form; reflects a newly-captured inbound message within one poll cycle when rendered on the form.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-022">PCF uses React 16/17 PLATFORM libraries — MUST NOT bundle React 18. Manifest declares platform libraries; the mounted tree is 16/17-compatible.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-006">PCF is for form binding — the control binds to the `sprk_communication`/thread record and resolves `threadId` from the bound context.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-026">Path-A exception — OOB form + PCF, NOT a Code Page. Cite in the deploy PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-04">The packaged bundle MUST NOT contain any `@azure/communication-*` dependency; grep/inspect the bundle. `@spaarke/auth` is consumed at the PCF boundary only, never inside the shared component.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Build with `npm run build:prod` (NOT `npm run build` — AP-1 / root §12). Pack + deploy the solution ZIP via the `pcf-deploy` skill.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Reuse the email-r4 `CommunicationActions`/`CommunicationConnections` PCF packaging + auth boundary; do not invent a new pattern (§11).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">No BFF publish-size / CVE obligations — client + deploy only (root §10 N/A).</constraint>
  </constraints>

