    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Virtual PCF mounting a shared component" location="src/client/pcf/CommunicationActions/">
        The email-r4 pattern: a PCF hosts a `@spaarke/ui-components` React component, wires PCF context → props, and consumes `@spaarke/auth` at the boundary. Mirror manifest + solution structure.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="ADR-022 platform libraries" location=".claude/adr/ADR-022-pcf-platform-libraries.md">
        Declare React/ReactDOM as platform libraries in the manifest; do not bundle React 18. The mounted component tree must be 16/17-compatible.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="pcf-deploy solution ZIP" location=".claude/skills/pcf-deploy/SKILL.md">
        `npm run build:prod` → pack solution → import via PAC. Place the control on the OOB form.
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps>
    <step order="1">Read `src/client/pcf/CommunicationActions/` + `CommunicationConnections/` (manifest, `index.ts`, `@spaarke/auth` boundary, solution ZIP layout), `src/client/pcf/CLAUDE.md`, `PCF-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md`, and ADR-022/ADR-006. Confirm the shared `CommunicationTimeline` props contract from task 060.</step>
    <step order="2">Scaffold `src/client/pcf/CommunicationTimeline/`: `ControlManifest.Input.xml` (bound to the thread/`sprk_communication` record; declare React/ReactDOM platform libraries per ADR-022; a `bffBaseUrl` property + env-var), `index.ts` implementing `init`/`updateView`/`destroy`.</step>
    <step order="3">In `index.ts`, resolve `threadId` from the bound record (the `sprk_thread` lookup or thread record id), build an `authenticatedFetch` via the Spaarke PCF `@spaarke/auth` pattern, read `bffBaseUrl`, and mount `&lt;CommunicationTimeline threadId authenticatedFetch bffBaseUrl pollIntervalMs /&gt;` via the platform React.</step>
    <step order="4">Verify React 16/17 compatibility of the mounted tree: run the PCF build; if a React-18-only API from 060 breaks under platform React, coordinate a shared-lib fix (do NOT fork). Grep the produced bundle for `@azure/communication` — MUST be absent (NFR-04).</step>
    <step order="5">Run `npm run build:prod` in the control folder (NOT `npm run build` — AP-1). Resolve any manifest/type errors.</step>
    <step order="6">Invoke the `pcf-deploy` skill: pack the solution ZIP + import to the target environment. Place the control on the OOB `sprk_communication`/thread main form (document the form + section placement).</step>
    <step order="7">Run UI tests via the `ui-test` skill against the deployed control (see `&lt;ui-tests&gt;`): renders without console errors; dark-mode correct; reflects a new inbound message within one poll cycle.</step>
    <step order="9.5">FULL-rigor quality gates: `code-review` on the PCF wrapper + manifest (focus: platform libraries declared, no React 18 bundled, no ACS SDK in the bundle, auth at the boundary only); `adr-check` against ADR-022/ADR-006/ADR-026 + `spec.md` (FR-10, NFR-04). Address Critical findings.</step>
    <step order="10">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (061 ✅) + `current-task.md`; record decisions (form + section placement, `threadId` resolution path, `bffBaseUrl` config mechanism, UI-test evidence, any shared-lib React-16/17 fix coordinated with 060).</step>
  </steps>

